## Findings

- **No public model named "GLM-5.2-Coding" exists** as of 2026-11-06:
  - Z.ai's official lineup is GLM-5, GLM-5.1, GLM-5.2, GLM-5.3 (open weights) — no separate `-coding` variant
  - OpenRouter: 404 for `z-ai/glm-5.2-coding` (only `z-ai/glm-5.2` exists)
  - No Hugging Face checkpoint, model card, or third-party listing found for a coding variant
  - The "GLM Coding Plan" is a flat-rate *subscription* serving `glm-5.2` (and later 5.3) — not a distinct model
- This slug is a `-coding` label **without a distinct vendor route** — exactly the phantom category RULES.md forbids scaffolding/researching.
- The underlying model is **GLM-5.2** (flagship, 2026-06-16; ~744–753B MoE / 40B active; 1M context; $1.40/$4.40; MIT license) — if the orchestrator wants this folder researched, it should point to `glm-5.2` (or confirm an actual coding-variant API ID exists).

